#: src/quick-start.md:1
msgid "Quick Start"
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start.md:3
msgid ""
"See the installation section for how to install `just` on your computer. Try "
"running `just --version` to make sure that it’s installed correctly."
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start.md:6
msgid ""
"For an overview of the syntax, check out [this cheatsheet](https://"
"cheatography.com/linux-china/cheat-sheets/justfile/)."
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start.md:9
msgid ""
"Once `just` is installed and working, create a file named `justfile` in the "
"root of your project with the following contents:"
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start.md:21
msgid ""
"When you invoke `just`, it looks for a file named `justfile` in the current "
"directory and upwards, so you can invoke it from any subdirectory of your "
"project."
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start.md:25
msgid ""
"The search for a `justfile` is case insensitive, so any case, like "
"`Justfile`, `JUSTFILE`, or `JuStFiLe`, will work. `just` will also look for "
"files with the name `.justfile`, in case you’d like to hide a `justfile`."
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start.md:29
msgid ""
"By default, running `just` with no arguments runs the first recipe in the "
"`justfile`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start.md:38
msgid "One or more arguments specify the recipe(s) to run:"
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start.md:45
msgid ""
"`just` prints each command to standard error before running it, which is why "
"`echo 'This is a recipe!'` was printed. This is suppressed for lines "
"starting with `@`, which is why `echo 'This is another recipe.'` was not "
"printed."
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start.md:49
msgid ""
"Recipes stop running if a command fails. Here `cargo publish` will only run "
"if `cargo test` succeeds:"
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start.md:59
msgid ""
"Recipes can depend on other recipes. Here the `test` recipe depends on the "
"`build` recipe, so `build` will run before `test`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start.md:62
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"build:\n"
"  cc main.c foo.c bar.c -o main\n"
"\n"
"test: build\n"
"  ./test\n"
"\n"
"sloc:\n"
"  @echo \"`wc -l *.c` lines of code\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start.md:80
msgid ""
"Recipes without dependencies will run in the order they’re given on the "
"command line:"
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start.md:89
msgid ""
"Dependencies will always run first, even if they are passed after a recipe "
"that depends on them:"
msgstr ""

#: src/quick-start.md:99
msgid "Recipes may depend on recipes in submodules:"
msgstr ""
